# ztd environment template.
#
# The ztd binary reads environment variables only through the typed keys in
# protocol/constants/env_vars.json (INV-ENV-04, docs/devs/devs.md). Host-native
# runs (make up, make gw, ./ztd ...) do not read this file: export variables in
# your shell or pass the matching ./ztd flags (`./ztd <command> --help`).
#
# Only secrets and user-specific endpoints or identities belong here. Platform
# configuration (ports, service URLs, passkey and CORS origins, consensus,
# doctrine and vault paths, models) is never an env setting: it is a typed
# default or a flag.
#
# No key is required for the host-native flow. Every key a supported flow reads
# is listed below as a commented entry with its purpose, its consumer, whether
# the default flow needs it, and an example value. CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN is a
# Go-only infrastructure key and is not listed here.
#
# Web search and LLM provider keys are configured in platform settings, not
# environment variables.
